"prose": [
{
"from": 133,
"to": 140,
"text": "The gates run the driver's unit tests, the new stand check, the existing checks that read kept checks (their reader changes), the committed checks' regeneration and its byte-equal reader, the doc leg for the new public items, and the local pre-push gate `fast` (fmt → clippy → workspace tests → CI scripts → embolden). No live leg: every check is an in-process cargo target or a seven_guis process check that owns its host. No smoke entry: the test plan declares no boot-smoke trigger paths and nothing launches an app or mints an id. The diff adds OS-conditional sites — the `cfg(unix)` items of `stand_explore` — so the plan carries the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries; the CI entry's note names the OS legs that witness them. The `coverage` (escher-driver's 97 % floor) and `stand-repeat` legs run in CI, read through that entry."
}
],
